  "foaf:name": "Citizens of the Sea: Mapping Ocean Health at Scale",
  "sdo:name": "Citizens of the Sea: Mapping Ocean Health at Scale",
  "sdo:description": "Citizens of the Sea (CitSea) is a New Zealand–based charitable trust building a citizen-powered ocean observing network to fill critical gaps in biodiversity knowledge. By equipping yachts, commercial vessels, and racing fleets with easy-to-use environmental DNA (eDNA) kits, CitSea generates large-scale, spatio-temporal datasets from offshore regions rarely studied. Each sample contributes to a growing bioarchive of eDNA, preserving genetic snapshots of marine life for reanalysis with future technologies. These resources provide governments, NGOs, and conservation communities with baselines to monitor species, detect climate-driven shifts, and strengthen management. CitSea ensures data sovereignty by returning results to jurisdictions, sharing them via interactive dashboards, and publishing in open-access repositories such as GBIF and OBIS. Beyond data, CitSea builds partnerships and public engagement, creating a legacy of science and stewardship.",
  "sdo:location": "New Zealand",
  "sdo:identifier": "81.9",
  "sdo:url": "https://oceandecade.org/actions/citizens-of-the-sea-mapping-ocean-health-at-scale/",
